    {
      "designator": "CS23-0",
      "grouping_at_time": "Subpart E \u2014 Powerplant",
      "title_at_revision": "Induction system screens",
      "text": "If induction system screens are used on reciprocating engines \u2013 (a) Each screen must be upstream of the carburettor or fuel injection system; (b) No screen may be in any part of the induction system that is the only passage through which air can reach the engine, unless \u2013 (1) The available preheat is at least 56\u00b0C (100\u00b0F); and (2) The screen can be de-iced by heated air; (c) No screen may be de-iced by alcohol alone; and (d) It must be impossible for fuel to strike any screen.",
      "publication_cite": "ED Decision 2003/014/RM",
